# Environment Variables

## Required for Production

### Form Submission API
```
VITE_FORM_API_URL=https://your-backend-api.com/api/signup
```
Set this to your backend API endpoint that will handle form submissions.

**Recommended services:**
- Formspree: https://formspree.io (easiest setup)
- EmailJS: https://www.emailjs.com
- Mailchimp API: for email list management
- SendGrid API: for email notifications
- Custom backend: Node.js/Express, Python/Flask, etc.

**Example Formspree setup:**
```
VITE_FORM_API_URL=https://formspree.io/f/YOUR_FORM_ID
```

### Instagram Feed (Optional)
```
VITE_INSTAGRAM_ACCESS_TOKEN=your_instagram_access_token
VITE_INSTAGRAM_USER_ID=your_instagram_user_id
```
Get these from Facebook Developer Console after setting up Instagram Basic Display API.
Tutorial: https://developers.facebook.com/docs/instagram-basic-display-api/getting-started

## Development

Create a `.env.local` file (not committed to git) with your local values:

```bash
cp .env.example .env.local
```

Then add your actual values to `.env.local`.

## Production Deployment

Set these environment variables in your hosting platform:
- Vercel: Project Settings > Environment Variables
- Netlify: Site Settings > Build & Deploy > Environment
- Render: Dashboard > Environment > Environment Variables
- GitHub Pages: Use GitHub Secrets for build actions

## Notes

- All Vite environment variables must start with `VITE_` to be accessible in the browser
- Never commit `.env.local` or any file containing actual secrets
- Rotate access tokens regularly for security
